    {
      "url": "https://andrewchincea.com/research/number-theory/",
      "title": "🐴 Analytic number theory · Andrew Chincea",
      "viewport": [
        1220,
        820
      ],
      "text": "RESEARCH\n\nAnalytic number theory\nIllustration\nAbout\n\nI study the largest kth-power divisor of a random integer.\n\nIn our submitted manuscript, \"Largest kth-Power Divisor of a Random Integer,\" Dr. Tsz Ho Chan and I establish an asymptotic formula with an O(log x) error term for every integer k ≥ 2.\n\nPosition\nUndergraduate Researcher – Analytic Number Theory, Kennesaw State University · Aug 2025 – Present\nAdvisor\nDr. Tsz Ho Chan\nMethods\nAsymptotic analysis of the largest kth-power divisor of a random integer.\nPython experiments on integers up to 10⁸, calculating empirical averages, growth constants and relative errors to validate the theoretical results.\nRelated work\n\nPAPERTsz Ho Chan and Andrew Chincea. Largest kth-Power Divisor of a Random Integer. Submitted.\n\nTALKAndrew Chincea and Michael Liu (Mar 2026). Largest Square Divisor of a Random Integer. Statistics & Data Applications session, 105th MAA Southeastern Section Meeting, University of North Alabama, Florence, AL.\n\nSee this area in the Garden →",
