    {
      "url": "https://andrewchincea.com/research/spectral-fractals/",
      "title": "🐴 Spectral analysis on fractals · Andrew Chincea",
      "viewport": [
        1220,
        820
      ],
      "text": "RESEARCH\n\nSpectral analysis on fractals\nIllustration\nAbout\n\nAs a First-Year Scholar, I studied eigenvalues of the fractal Laplacian.\n\nI looked at how fractal geometry shapes the spectrum of the fractal Laplacian. I started from the Dirichlet eigenvalue problem in one dimension and then extended the analysis to two.\n\nPosition\nFirst-Year Scholar Undergraduate Researcher, Kennesaw State University · Aug 2024 – May 2025\nMethods\nFormulated the Dirichlet eigenvalue problem for the one-dimensional fractal Laplacian and derived analytical solutions for specific fractal parameters.\nComputed eigenvalues and eigenfunctions numerically to show how fractal geometry shapes the spectrum.\nExtended the analysis to two dimensions using separation of variables.\nRelated work\n\nPOSTERAndrew Chincea (Mar 2025). Properties of Eigenvalues of Fractal Laplacian. 104th MAA Southeastern Section Meeting, High Point University, High Point, NC.\n\nSee this area in the Garden →",
