      ],
      "text": "About\n\nI'm an undergraduate at Kennesaw State University, working toward a B.S. in Mathematics (Statistics concentration) and a B.S. in Data Science and Analytics. I work in analytic number theory and on predicting water quality on river networks. As a First-Year Scholar, I studied spectral analysis on fractals. I'm interested in PhD programs and in mathematics and data science REUs.\n\nYou can also browse my research areas, selected work in the Garden, or my CV.\n\nContact\nEmail\nachincea@students.kennesaw.edu\nGitHub\ngithub.com/andrewc156\nLinkedIn\nwww.linkedin.com/in/andrewchincea",
